{"_meta": {"name": "topic requests and controls", "version": 2, "created": "2026-10-25", "rows": 38, "tuning": "dev set for the topic-search feature (written before the feature exists); the feature will be built against it, so treat its numbers as in-sample", "label": "topic feature dev set: topic rows need the pipeline to expose matched subjects", "how_built": "Topic rows: hand-written natural requests with the topic words a matching work's subjects should contain (folded substring). Control rows: real titles/authors that contain request or topic words; canonical work = live GET /search.json?title=&author=&sort=editions on 2026-10-25 (12 calls), most-edited work whose main title equals the title; extra ids only for other records of the same book (see note).", "scoring": "topic rows: status ambiguous with reason topic_search, and at least min_topic_hits of the top 5 shown have a subject matching a topic word (folded; a whole word with an optional s/es plural, or a prefix when the word ends with *; phrases match as phrases); top-1 = the first shown has one. control rows: scored like golden rows (strict work ids; status match or ambiguous). topic_author rows (topic + author with few or no hits): status only (ambiguous or none); any match is a false positive.", "changelog": [{"version": 1, "date": "2026-10-25", "change": "21 topic requests + 12 controls"}, {"version": 2, "date": "2026-10-25", "change": "added books about bears and wolves; books about foxes; books about space for kids; Novel on Yellow Paper by Stevie Smith; books about cats by isaac asimov. 'picture books about trains' and 'a novel set in paris' were requested too but are already rows topic-10 and topic-03.", "reason": "lead: Codex review of the topic feature found edge cases (two topics, plural fox/wolves, topic + author with no hits, a title that reads like a topic frame)"}]}}
